       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for 50 mg. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, that dose is five times the maximum and could cause serious harm. That includes profound hypotension, shock, and pulmonary edema, and the effects could last for days because amlodipine has a half-life of 30\u201350 hours.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 5 mg once daily, titrating to 10 mg if needed. If you want faster blood pressure control, I can add a note for reassessment this afternoon or at evening rounds.\n- **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't enough, combining classes is the usual approach. Tell me which drug and dose and I'll enter it.\n- **Consult pharmacy.** If there is an unusual clinical reason for the high dose, pharmacy review and documentation of the rationale would normally come first.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
